'''Zombie Survival''' is a cross-platform [[Special:MyLanguage/:Category:Game worlds|game world]] published by {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_b22687ae-091a-4001-ae15-c9dabc844645|Τeal}} Players fight zombie hordes.

== Layout ==

Players spawn in a lobby. The lobby has Start Game, map select, difficulty select, and mode select. It has a Shooting Range, a mirror, language settings (English, 日本語, and 简体中文), credits, Open Store, Discord, a Patreon link, FPS and graphics settings, and a supporter board.

A height check measures the avatar. Players who join a game in progress wait for the next round.

== Gameplay ==

Money buys weapons, upgrades, ammunition, and area unlocks. Levels and EXP are cosmetic.

=== Maps ===

The maps are Abandoned City, Frozen Frontier, and Cave Cove. Each map has highscore boards for Casual, Normal, and Nightmare.

=== Modes and difficulties ===

Modes are Standard and Boss Rush. Boss Rush has a 2.5× zombie scaling multiplier.

Difficulties are Casual, Normal, and Nightmare. Casual has a control labeled Disable Safe Zone.

The game master can disable the Safe Zone, emergency restart a round, cut rest time to 30 seconds, allow players to pick up weapons after death, and randomize vending machines.

=== Weapons and upgrades ===

The starting pistol is the M1911. Other weapons can be shared. Dropped weapons the player owns are blue. Dropped weapons other players own are yellow. A Max Ammo pickup refills all weapons, including weapons on the ground. An upgrade station increases fire power and ammunition.

Hip reload is pointing the gun up or down to reload. A two-handed grab uses the off-hand and improves recoil control.

Weapon shop prices change during a match. The BB Gun is a world-store listing.

